course: dictionary
lesson: 11264
title: Wrath: very great anger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wrath is a strong, old-fashioned word for very great anger. You will meet it in Bible stories and old tales, where kings, gods and storms can show wrath. «A gentle answer turns away wrath» is a line from Proverbs. It means a calm reply can stop someone's anger from growing.
explain: Today we also use wrath as a joke. «I'll face my teacher's wrath» means you expect to be told off for something you did wrong. Look at the clues around the word. Words like harsh and stirs up show that the anger is strong and could get worse.
fact: Wrath means very great anger, and it is a noun.
fact: «The wrath of God» is God's anger at evil and sin, as described in many Bible stories.
fact: In ethics, wrath is one of the seven deadly sins, also called anger.
fact: «Face someone's wrath» means having to deal with their anger, often because you did something wrong.
fact: Wrath is formal and old-fashioned, so in everyday talk people usually say anger.
exercise: «A gentle answer turns away wrath, but a harsh word stirs up anger.» What does wrath mean here? | A gentle breeze | A kind friend | A loud song | *Very great anger
exercise: «I'll face my teacher's wrath.» What does this joke mean? | You will teach the class a new song | You will ask for a holiday | *You expect to be told off by your teacher | You are going to be very happy
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to wrath? | Gentle | Breakfast | *Anger | Whisper
test: In Bible stories, «the wrath of God» is God's anger at what? | Sweets and cake | The weather in spring | *Evil and sin | Lost keys
test: Why might Proverbs say «A gentle answer turns away wrath»? | Shouting makes friends happy | Anger is good for you | Answers should always be long | *A calm reply can stop someone getting angry
exam: What is the best explanation of wrath? | A kind of cake | *Very great anger, often formal or old-fashioned | A happy holiday | A small, gentle wind
